      "judge_rationale": "Overall the candidate summary is largely accurate and faithful to the provided source material: it preserves the major claims about traditional (callous) toughness, Bobby Knight’s accomplishments and abusive methods, Baumrind’s responsiveness vs. demandingness framework and the three parenting styles, the Jordan McNair case and rhabdomyolysis risk from extreme workouts, the harms of authoritarian approaches, and the contrast with coaches like Pete Carroll and research favoring trust/inclusion. It keeps most critical qualifiers (e.g., that Knight’s performance record is real but his methods are abusive; that authoritarian methods have psychological consequences rather than necessarily physical death in homes/classrooms) and conveys the core mechanism contrasts (fake/callous vs. real/navigational toughness).\n\nDeductions: the summary inserts a few elements that are not clearly present in the provided excerpt/rubric (notably the exact four pillar titles and the closing Rich Roll quote), which reduces faithfulness and coverage scores. It also omits a few small source details (e.g., the summary does not mention Knight’s five Final Four appearances) and tightens some language in ways that slightly overstate universals. These issues prevent perfect scores but the summary remains a strong, well-structured representation of the source.",
